}

docs {
  # GET /course-contents/{id}
  
  Retrieves the curriculum tree (topics → lessons / quizzes / assignments).
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `GET`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/course-contents/:id`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **With API key + JWT:** user must be able to view the course.
  - **Without API key:** allowed only when the course is **public**.
  - **Required Permission (API key):** `Read`, `Read/Write`, or `All`
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `id` | `integer` | **Yes** | Course post ID. |
  
  ## Notes
  
  When learning payloads cannot be revealed, topic `summary` is empty and content items are outline-only (no `post_content`).
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK (Success)
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_course",
    "message": "Course contents retrieved successfully",
    "data": [
      {
        "id": 201,
        "title": "Module 1: Introduction to Web APIs",
        "summary": "Overview of REST architecture and HTTP fundamentals.",
        "contents": [
          {
            "ID": 301,
            "post_title": "Lesson 1: What is a REST API?",
            "post_content": "Detailed overview text...",
            "post_name": "what-is-a-rest-api",
            "post_type": "lesson",
            "menu_order": 0
          },
          {
            "ID": 302,
            "post_title": "Quiz 1: HTTP Basics",
            "post_content": "Test your knowledge of status codes.",
            "post_name": "quiz-1-http-basics",
            "post_type": "tutor_quiz",
            "menu_order": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ### 404 Not Found
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_course",
    "message": "Contents for this course with the given course id not found",
    "data": []
  }
  ```
}
